    "text": "A black body emits radiation at the rate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> when its temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. At this temperature the wavelength at which the radiation has a maximum intensity is&nbsp;<math><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi> <mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math>. If at another temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>'</mo></math> the power radiated is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>'</mo></math> and wavelength at maximum intensity is <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mo>/</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;then",
